+# psi fork workspace (inside tmnl repo)
+
+This directory is a staging area to manage forks/submodules for pi upstream work.
+
+## Enumerated upstream repos (via `gh`)
+
+Current query used:
+
+```bash
+gh repo list badlogic --limit 500 --json name,nameWithOwner,url | \
+  jq -r '.[] | select(.name|test("^pi(-|$)")) | [.nameWithOwner,.url] | @tsv'
+```
+
+Mapped repos are in [`repos.json`](./repos.json).
+
+## One-command sync
+
+```bash
+bash psi/sync-forks-and-submodules.sh psi
+```
+
+This script will:
+1. Fork each upstream repo to `psi/<mapped-name>`
+2. Add each fork as a git submodule under `psi/submodules/<mapped-name>`
+3. Add `upstream` remote in each submodule clone
+
+## Permission note
+
+Creating repos under `psi/*` requires GitHub permissions for owner `psi`.
+If you get permission errors, either:
+- run with an owner you control, e.g. `bash psi/sync-forks-and-submodules.sh <your-owner>`
+- or grant your token/account repo-create access in `psi`.
